2	//! parsing.
3	//!
4	//! v1.2 (Phase 2): a single `Tool` struct covers both the COR24
5	//! assembler (`cor24-run --assemble`) and the p-code assembler
6	//! (`pa24r <input> -o <output>`). The kind is carried in
7	//! `ToolKind`; `build()` dispatches the argv accordingly.
8	//! Combining them into one struct keeps `tool.rs` under
9	//! sw-checklist's per-module function-count budget.
10	//!
11	//! `from_source` resolves the v1.2 schema's `[tools.<n>.source]`
12	//! kinds: `Path`, `FromPath { binary }`, `Sibling { path,
13	//! artifact }`. `Vendor` waits for Phase 4.
14	//!
15	//! The cache is in-memory and per-process: a single `sw-launch`
16	//! invocation that needs the same artifact twice spawns the tool
17	//! exactly once. Disk-persistent caching is Phase 4 work.
